            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0588" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.34/4–2346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-26T19:00:00-05:00">April 26, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>223. Your 416 Apr 23.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d522-f1"/> Sale by Navy of heavier
                    vessels to Chile must await enabling legislation. It is hoped that such
                    legislation may be submitted to Congress in the near future. Pending passage of
                    legislation impossible set any date for sale or cost of vessels desired by
                    Chile. Navy Dept advises cannot for personnel and budgetary reasons hold open to
                    Chile offer of small vessels enumerated in Deptel 206, Apr. 12. Understand Navy Dept has telegraphed Chief of
                    US Mission in above sense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
